  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Electrical Contractors and Other Wiring Installation Contractors (NAICS 238210) received $482M in federal contract obligations in FY2026 to date. The market recorded 2,066 awards with an average award size of $233K. Obligations fell 39.1% year over year. Annual obligations were larger in prior fiscal years, with FY21 at $792M, FY22 at $853M, FY23 at $945M, FY24 at $824M, and FY25 at $791M. The Department of Defense, the Department of Veterans Affairs, and the Department of State are the top buyers in FY2026 to date, and XATOR LLC, SINTELA INC, and WSP USA SOLUTIONS INC lead vendors by obligation. The note states that all figures are contract obligations and current-year totals are partial, fiscal year to date. Capture teams and contractors should treat FY2026 to date as an incomplete picture because timing differences in award flow can create large year-over-year changes when comparing fiscal-year-to-date snapshots to full prior fiscal years. Use the listed agency and vendor obligations to prioritize outreach and competitive positioning this fiscal year to date.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "Why did obligations fall 39.1% year over year?",
        "body": "Obligations fell 39.1% year over year, which indicates a smaller FY2026 to date intake. The Department of Defense obligated $131M and the Department of Veterans Affairs obligated $112M in FY2026 to date, so agency timing and award pacing are key drivers. Current-year totals are partial, fiscal year to date, so timing shifts can make large percentage moves versus prior full fiscal years."
